From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Kevin Turcios <turcioskevinr@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 00:34:08 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Learn the target interpreter

pip works for the interpreter running it. The compiled kpip has none of
its own: sys.executable, sys.prefix, sys.path and sysconfig describe the
bundle it was built with. kpip._internal.interpreters says which Python
kpip installs for and what it is: the Python running kpip, read live, when
kpip runs from source; otherwise one found the way uv finds it --
--python, VIRTUAL_ENV, a non-base CONDA_PREFIX, a .venv here or above,
conda base, python3 or python on PATH -- and read by running a probe with
it. The probe carries the vendored packaging's tag modules, so a probed
interpreter's wheel tags are exactly its own. Answers are kept in the
cache until the interpreter or its search path changes.

Nothing reads it yet; later patches move pip's uses of the running
interpreter onto it.
